      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dynamic strength–ductility balance of Co-free FeNiCrMn is governed by temperature- and strain-rate-dependent dislocation-avalanche dynamics.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4655315::web::023::comparison_of_experiments_to_model_predi",
        "PMC4655315::web::030::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intrinsic chemical disorder in Co-free FeNiCrMn creates a distinct distribution of weak dislocation sources.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4655315::web::023::comparison_of_experiments_to_model_predi",
        "PMC4655315::web::030::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Acoustic-emission monitoring and high-resolution stress–strain profiling can be used concurrently to characterize dislocation avalanches.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slip serrations are expected within approximately 100–600 K and strain rates of 10^-4 to 10^-1 s^-1.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4655315::web::023::comparison_of_experiments_to_model_predi",
        "PMC4655315::web::030::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant structural mediator is the amplitude and frequency distribution of dislocation avalanches observed as slip serrations.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4655315::web::023::comparison_of_experiments_to_model_predi",
        "PMC4655315::web::030::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Weak dislocation sources activate during slip and subsequently heal or re-strengthen between avalanches.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4655315::web::023::comparison_of_experiments_to_model_predi",
        "PMC4655315::web::030::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The activation and healing rates of weak dislocation sources are highly sensitive to both temperature and strain rate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4655315::web::023::comparison_of_experiments_to_model_predi",
        "PMC4655315::web::030::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Avalanche behavior modulates strain hardening and ductility by altering the yield response.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At low temperatures and high strain rates, Co-free FeNiCrMn will exhibit larger but less frequent avalanches than equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The larger, less frequent avalanches at low temperatures and high strain rates will produce a higher yield stress.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At high temperatures and low strain rates, Co-free FeNiCrMn will exhibit more frequent, smaller slip events than equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "More frequent, smaller slip events will reduce stress hysteresis and enhance ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline is equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi tested under the same temperature and strain-rate conditions.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4655315::web::030::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is restricted to the single-phase FCC regime from approximately 100–600 K and 10^-4 to 10^-1 s^-1.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At strain rates outside the stated range, additional mechanisms such as phonon drag may influence deformation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
